WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.966 --> 00:00:15.407
Mother carried Peter inside.

2
00:00:16.388 --> 00:00:18.470
His foot was bleeding, and his face was pale.

3
00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.252
Dr. Forest bandaged his foot.

4
00:00:22.273 --> 00:00:23.554
Bobbie whispered to the doctor.

5
00:00:23.574 --> 00:00:27.898
"He won't be lame, or have to use crutches forever, will he?"

6
00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:30.320
The doctor told her not to worry.

7
00:00:32.828 --> 00:00:36.331
Over the next week, Peter rested and Phyllis played in the garden.

8
00:00:37.352 --> 00:00:38.973
Meanwhile Bobbie thought about Father.

9
00:00:40.014 --> 00:00:41.275
Why was he still away?

10
00:00:42.315 --> 00:00:44.217
Was there something that Mother wasn't telling them?

11
00:00:46.118 --> 00:00:48.340
The answer to Bobbie's questions came the next day.

12
00:00:49.961 --> 00:00:52.223
She went to the station to get magazines for Peter.

13
00:00:53.063 --> 00:00:56.366
They were old magazines that people had left on trains or in the waiting room.

14
00:00:57.407 --> 00:00:58.928
Perks said the children could have them.

15
00:01:00.336 --> 00:01:04.900
"I'll put some newspaper and string around the magazines to keep them together," Perks said.

16
00:01:05.921 --> 00:01:09.163
He took an old newspaper from the pile and wrapped up the magazines.

17
00:01:10.685 --> 00:01:14.468
On the way home, Bobbie stopped at the train crossing as a train went past.

18
00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:19.151
Bobbie rested the parcel on the crossing gate.

19
00:01:20.172 --> 00:01:24.176
She looked down at the newspaper on top and started to read a headline and It was like

20
00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:24.996
a horrible dream.

21
00:01:26.377 --> 00:01:29.360
Bobbie ran home, went to her room, and locked the door.

22
00:01:31.004 --> 00:01:33.345
Inside her room Bobbie took out the newspaper again.

23
00:01:34.445 --> 00:01:37.847
The front page said: Five Years in Prison for Spy!

24
00:01:38.967 --> 00:01:41.068
And the name of the "spy" was her father.

25
00:01:41.088 --> 00:01:44.710
"So now I know," she whispered to herself.

26
00:01:47.851 --> 00:01:50.552
Then Bobbie had to eat dinner and pretend that nothing was wrong.

27
00:01:51.853 --> 00:01:54.214
She tried, but she wasn't very successful.

28
00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:56.775
Her eyes were red from crying.

29
00:01:56.795 --> 00:01:58.815
"Is anything wrong?"

30
00:01:59.236 --> 00:01:59.976
Mother asked her.

31
00:02:01.064 --> 00:02:02.545
"I'm all right," Bobbie said.

32
00:02:04.426 --> 00:02:06.348
After dinner Mother went to Bobbie's room.

33
00:02:07.429 --> 00:02:08.229
"What's the matter?"

34
00:02:08.629 --> 00:02:09.390
she wanted to know.

35
00:02:10.491 --> 00:02:12.212
Bobbie showed her mother the newspaper.

36
00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:14.914
"Oh, Bobbie!"

37
00:02:15.354 --> 00:02:15.914
cried Mother.

38
00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:18.416
"You don't believe it, do you?

39
00:02:19.497 --> 00:02:21.258
You don't think Daddy is a spy!"

40
00:02:21.278 --> 00:02:24.580
"No!" Bobbie said.

41
00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:29.584
"He's good and honest and he has done nothing wrong," said Mother.

42
00:02:30.636 --> 00:02:31.857
"We must remember that."

43
00:02:32.918 --> 00:02:33.678
"What happened?"

44
00:02:34.059 --> 00:02:34.719
asked Bobbie.

45
00:02:34.739 --> 00:02:38.542
"Do you remember those two men who came to see Father?"

46
00:02:38.962 --> 00:02:39.422
said Mother.

47
00:02:39.442 --> 00:02:46.407
"Well, they said he was a spy, and that he'd sold government secrets to another country.

48
00:02:47.468 --> 00:02:49.950
There were some letters in Daddy's desk at his office.

49
00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:54.133
When the police saw them, they were sure Daddy was a spy."

50
00:02:54.153 --> 00:02:57.735
"But why were the letters in his desk?"

51
00:02:58.115 --> 00:02:59.848
asked Bobbie.

52
00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:04.612
"Somebody put them there," replied Mother, "and that person is the real spy."

53
00:03:04.632 --> 00:03:07.213
"Who?" asked Bobbie.

54
00:03:07.233 --> 00:03:09.155
"We don't know."

55
00:03:09.175 --> 00:03:13.978
"Can't you explain that Daddy is not a spy to the police?"

56
00:03:14.459 --> 00:03:14.999
said Bobbie.

57
00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:19.622
"We tried, but they won't listen," said Mother sadly.

58
00:03:19.642 --> 00:03:22.184
"I've tried everything.

59
00:03:23.345 --> 00:03:24.606
All we can do is wait.

60
00:03:25.747 --> 00:03:29.713
Now we can't talk about this anymore, and we can't tell Peter or Phyllis.

61
00:03:30.733 --> 00:03:32.274
Please be brave, Bobbie."

62
00:03:34.015 --> 00:03:36.075
Bobbie had to try to help Father somehow.

63
00:03:37.276 --> 00:03:38.837
She wrote a letter to the old gentleman.

64
00:03:39.877 --> 00:03:42.558
He had helped them before—maybe he could help them again.

65
00:03:43.919 --> 00:03:46.360
Dear Friend, Please read the newspaper.

66
00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:50.541
The story is about our father, but it is not true.

67
00:03:51.982 --> 00:03:56.364
Mother says someone put the letters in Father's desk, but nobody listens to her.

68
00:03:57.504 --> 00:03:58.864
You are good and clever.

69
00:03:59.825 --> 00:04:01.145
Can you find the real spy?

70
00:04:02.245 --> 00:04:04.646
Peter and Phyllis don't know Father is in prison.

71
00:04:05.726 --> 00:04:06.387
Please help me.

72
00:04:07.387 --> 00:04:13.749
With love from your friend, Bobbie Bobbie tore the first page from the newspaper and put it in

73
00:04:13.789 --> 00:04:14.849
the envelope with her letter.

74
00:04:15.949 --> 00:04:19.410
She asked the stationmaster to please give it to the old gentleman the next morning.

75
00:04:20.611 --> 00:04:22.071
Now all she could do was wait.

76
00:04:23.131 --> 00:04:25.172
Would the old gentleman help her family again?
